WEBVTT

00:06.172 --> 00:08.174
[theme music playing]

01:03.313 --> 01:05.982
GENIE, MAKE A WISH

01:06.858 --> 01:08.485
I told you to prove it to me.

01:08.568 --> 01:11.071
Prove that humans are bound to be corrupt.

01:11.696 --> 01:13.073
This is my first wish.

01:16.367 --> 01:17.660
I've been tempted by you.

01:21.039 --> 01:23.041
You'd bet your life
on something as fragile…

01:24.709 --> 01:26.127
as the goodness of humanity?

01:26.211 --> 01:28.463
Wow! [scoffs] This is unbelievable.

01:30.840 --> 01:33.384
You will lose no matter what.
Just wait and see.

01:33.468 --> 01:36.304
I'll see to it that you lose.
You'll be begging me to please--

01:36.387 --> 01:38.056
Save it for when you actually win.

01:39.224 --> 01:40.266
And wear this.

01:43.144 --> 01:44.896
No, I'm going to celebrate early.

01:46.564 --> 01:47.816
I decide when to do what.

01:49.317 --> 01:52.111
Get a move on, human.
Spring nights are short.

01:55.031 --> 01:58.576
[Ka-young] If you were, in fact,
locked up for 983 years,

01:58.660 --> 02:00.912
how are you the most famous genie?

02:01.704 --> 02:04.874
I was famous even before I was locked up
for defying his orders.

02:04.958 --> 02:06.209
Why did you do that?

02:07.377 --> 02:08.419
You've tempted me.

02:08.503 --> 02:10.171
I was tempted… No. [clears throat]

02:12.549 --> 02:15.760
I refused to bow my head
to a lowly human molded from clay.

02:16.302 --> 02:17.846
-Look, 1,000 won!
-Where?

02:19.180 --> 02:20.682
[comical music playing]

02:22.308 --> 02:24.060
I was just tying my laces.

02:25.311 --> 02:26.521
[hums]

02:29.440 --> 02:31.151
Take your time tying them.

02:31.776 --> 02:33.945
Tie them to your heart's content.

02:36.447 --> 02:37.866
I swear I'll corrupt you,

02:38.449 --> 02:40.702
even if it's the last thing I do.

02:40.785 --> 02:42.954
I will wring your neck, you hear?

02:43.454 --> 02:46.624
I'll hang your head
at the gates of hell, and…

02:47.500 --> 02:48.918
[Im-seon] Is that you, Ka-young?

02:51.671 --> 02:52.672
Huh?

02:54.591 --> 02:57.093
Here comes the first human
to be corrupted.

02:57.635 --> 02:59.721
I should come by for an oil change.

03:00.972 --> 03:02.599
I'll stop by on my next day off.

03:02.682 --> 03:04.267
Sure. Come by.

03:06.477 --> 03:10.106
Kang Im-seon. A supermarket employee
and Granny An's eldest daughter-in-law.

03:10.189 --> 03:12.859
Huh. I know that kind of face well.

03:13.359 --> 03:15.987
The face of someone
who wants the world to end tomorrow.

03:16.070 --> 03:17.030
[cell phone chimes]

03:17.113 --> 03:19.032
[mysterious music playing]

03:21.159 --> 03:21.993
Gu Bo-gyeong.

03:23.286 --> 03:26.164
A bank employee.
We were classmates until high school.

03:30.585 --> 03:33.755
Did you get a text from the bank
about our new towel sets?

03:36.507 --> 03:38.843
I'm sure you use nicer ones, but still.

03:42.847 --> 03:45.225
-Are you going somewhere?
-I'm not. Go ahead.

03:45.308 --> 03:46.142
What?

03:47.310 --> 03:48.144
Okay.

03:54.275 --> 03:56.319
I know that kind of face well too.

03:56.402 --> 03:59.405
The face of someone who wants
the world to end as soon as today.

04:05.203 --> 04:07.205
So two are confirmed for corruption.

04:07.872 --> 04:10.208
-[dog growls, barks]
-[gasps]

04:14.837 --> 04:17.507
Oh, another familiar face, I see.

04:18.132 --> 04:20.802
What, do I not smell like
I belong in this neighborhood?

04:20.885 --> 04:22.262
Do I reek of oil?

04:22.345 --> 04:24.138
[barking]

04:24.889 --> 04:27.892
It's barking at you.
Did you take the hair clip out?

04:29.310 --> 04:30.311
Take a look.

04:31.104 --> 04:34.190
Dogs are spiritual animals,
so they can see me in any form.

04:34.274 --> 04:35.316
-Really?
-Hmm?

04:35.400 --> 04:37.068
-Paw-sitively fascinating.
-[dog barking]

04:37.151 --> 04:39.362
Of all the village dogs,
this one barks at me the most.

04:39.445 --> 04:41.614
-[barking continues]
-Really?

04:42.198 --> 04:44.742
I guess that makes you
tonight's third wishmaker.

04:44.826 --> 04:46.744
Nice to meet you, mutt.

04:47.870 --> 04:50.415
What a load of dog shit.
Dogs aren't included.

04:52.625 --> 04:53.626
Why not?

04:54.127 --> 04:57.046
You said the first five
we meet on this road.

04:57.130 --> 05:00.049
That should include all living beings.
Those are the rules.

05:00.133 --> 05:02.302
Don't you agree,
Ki Ka-young, lover of rules?

05:02.927 --> 05:03.928
[scoffs]

05:04.554 --> 05:06.723
THIS WAY TO CHEONGPUNG VILLAGE HALL

05:10.476 --> 05:11.311
Ms. Ki?

05:11.894 --> 05:13.479
Where are you headed this late?

05:13.980 --> 05:16.190
It's dangerous to be out alone at night.

05:17.275 --> 05:18.109
Need a lift?

05:18.192 --> 05:19.068
No, thanks.

05:19.569 --> 05:21.988
I'm not alone, and I'm meeting someone.

05:26.492 --> 05:28.244
Is that so? Take care, then.

05:33.624 --> 05:34.834
[Iblis] Huh?

05:34.917 --> 05:36.085
Eom Sang-tae.

05:36.586 --> 05:39.672
You know the gamja-tang spot?
He's the son of Granny Sa, the owner.

05:39.756 --> 05:43.718
Eom Sang-tae must not know
that you're the truly dangerous one here.

05:43.801 --> 05:46.512
Of course he does.
The entire village knows about me.

05:47.722 --> 05:50.224
But he probably doesn't know what I know.

05:51.142 --> 05:52.018
[scoffs]

05:53.936 --> 05:56.272
-Yikes, you scared me.
-[Iblis] Hmm?

05:57.774 --> 05:59.358
You must be out on a walk

05:59.942 --> 06:01.611
in the dead of night. [chuckles nervously]

06:01.694 --> 06:03.654
How's your YouTube channel doing?

06:04.363 --> 06:06.741
-Is Da-jin well?
-[man] Choi Da-jin, lock the doors!

06:06.824 --> 06:08.367
Only joking. [chuckles]

06:09.035 --> 06:10.745
Good night, then.

06:16.292 --> 06:18.628
I guess it must have been
about a year ago.

06:19.128 --> 06:21.339
He moved here for the farm life.

06:21.422 --> 06:23.716
He and his wife run a YouTube channel.

06:24.509 --> 06:26.260
So I guess we have our five.

06:27.136 --> 06:28.137
It's the best of five.

06:28.221 --> 06:30.181
I'll make it a clean sweep.

06:31.516 --> 06:32.767
You'll see it in no time.

06:32.850 --> 06:34.519
Those five will hit rock bottom.

06:36.312 --> 06:37.939
And that bottom is quite deep.

06:38.523 --> 06:40.817
Humans only realize their true colors

06:41.901 --> 06:43.903
when faced with the prospect of wishes.

06:44.987 --> 06:45.863
Is that so?

06:46.656 --> 06:48.658
And what does my wish say about me?

06:50.159 --> 06:51.577
That you're a psychopath.

06:53.830 --> 06:57.041
With a single wish, you led
four humans and a creature to corruption.

06:58.751 --> 06:59.585
Oh.

07:00.336 --> 07:02.296
And I forgot to mention something.

07:03.172 --> 07:06.175
There are both good and evil genies.

07:06.926 --> 07:09.887
Of them, there is one who conjures hell.

07:11.222 --> 07:12.515
They call him

07:12.598 --> 07:13.850
"Iblis"

07:14.350 --> 07:16.811
or "Shaytan."

07:18.312 --> 07:20.106
To use a name you may recognize…

07:22.358 --> 07:23.192
it's "Satan."

07:23.276 --> 07:24.819
[captivating music playing]

07:27.447 --> 07:28.531
It appears as though…

07:31.033 --> 07:32.869
I have encountered an evil genie.

07:34.245 --> 07:36.080
[crows cawing]

07:36.164 --> 07:37.999
[rats squeaking]

07:42.170 --> 07:44.046
[laughing]

07:54.557 --> 07:56.559
[captivating music continues]

08:24.003 --> 08:24.962
[music ends]

08:25.046 --> 08:26.547
[Sade] What are you going to do now?

08:26.631 --> 08:29.967
Even in this life,
she used her first wish selflessly.

08:30.468 --> 08:32.595
It wasn't exactly selfless, was it?

08:32.678 --> 08:35.932
She bet her life on people being kind.
What else is that but selflessness?

08:36.015 --> 08:38.100
And what did you call her? "A psychopath"?

08:38.184 --> 08:40.186
"I am Satan"?
What's with the sudden honesty?

08:40.269 --> 08:42.688
So the rats are
surprisingly accurate informants.

08:43.898 --> 08:44.941
[whimpers]

08:46.859 --> 08:48.736
I just didn't want to lose.

08:50.196 --> 08:51.072
What should I do?

08:51.989 --> 08:53.824
Maybe I should just skip this life?

08:54.659 --> 08:56.702
Ki Ka-young will live until 80 at most.

08:59.121 --> 09:02.208
With this lamp and those aluminum kettles,
those years should fly by.

09:02.291 --> 09:04.126
And how would you fund that habit?

09:04.919 --> 09:07.213
Yes, good plan. Let's just skip this life.

09:07.296 --> 09:09.507
For now, I'll try my best to avoid her.

09:10.007 --> 09:12.552
You go get a job at her auto shop
and gather some intel.

09:12.635 --> 09:13.469
What do you think?

09:13.553 --> 09:16.722
Right, so you'll be using my money.

09:17.557 --> 09:19.267
But where will you hide, Master?

09:22.436 --> 09:24.313
Somewhere very far away from here.

09:25.481 --> 09:26.899
Somewhere closer to him.

09:27.441 --> 09:29.443
[whimsical music playing]

09:34.198 --> 09:36.450
-[music ends]
-[door opens, closes]

09:36.534 --> 09:38.160
Come on out. Let's eat.

09:38.244 --> 09:39.579
No, I was just rushing out…

09:40.079 --> 09:42.707
Hey, that!
I know the perfect place to eat that.

09:43.583 --> 09:46.127
And don't tell Ka-young
that you saw me. Tsk.

09:53.759 --> 09:56.679
-[groans, sighs]
-[whistling]

09:58.055 --> 09:59.015
[whooshes]

09:59.098 --> 10:01.017
[amusing music playing]

10:08.232 --> 10:09.233
Mmm-hmm.

10:11.777 --> 10:12.778
How delicious.

10:16.907 --> 10:19.035
[dramatic music playing]

10:21.078 --> 10:22.496
[pilot 1] What? Status report?

10:22.580 --> 10:25.249
[pilot 2 in Japanese] I have just spotted
an unidentified flying object!

10:25.333 --> 10:26.167
[chuckles]

10:26.917 --> 10:28.502
I see a carpet. Over!

10:29.754 --> 10:30.671
Whoa!

10:32.131 --> 10:33.549
[in Korean] He's eating bibimbap. Over.

10:33.633 --> 10:36.135
[in Japanese] What are you talking about?
Give me a proper report!

10:37.345 --> 10:38.179
Mmm-hmm.

10:40.348 --> 10:41.182
Mmm?

10:42.433 --> 10:43.392
Hmm?

10:43.476 --> 10:45.478
[in Korean] What's the matter?
Come on, what is it?

10:45.978 --> 10:46.812
Huh?

10:48.564 --> 10:50.775
Oh, did you two arrange to meet here?

10:50.858 --> 10:51.776
Okay!

10:51.859 --> 10:53.569
[pilot 1] He's escaping.
Awaiting orders. Over.

10:53.653 --> 10:55.488
[pilot 2 in Japanese]
Should we shoot him down? Over!

10:55.571 --> 10:57.990
[reporter in Korean]
At around 3:38 p.m. today,

10:58.074 --> 11:01.619
the Ministry of National Defense
reported an unidentified flying object

11:01.702 --> 11:05.498
near the Korea-Japan maritime border,
which prompted a fighter jet standoff.

11:05.581 --> 11:09.585
They avoided providing specific details
regarding the unidentified flying object.

11:14.340 --> 11:17.051
I guess I've identified
the unidentified flying object.

11:18.219 --> 11:19.387
With my very eyes.

11:19.470 --> 11:21.806
I needed some time to myself
to mull things over.

11:22.598 --> 11:23.974
-[thuds]
-Shut it.

11:24.058 --> 11:26.811
You almost sparked a war
between two countries,

11:27.561 --> 11:29.313
then tucked into an in-flight meal?

11:30.106 --> 11:31.190
Bibimbap!

11:32.858 --> 11:34.610
Ms. Ki. You're hiring, aren't you?

11:40.950 --> 11:42.368
Please hire me for the job.

11:42.451 --> 11:44.495
I was practically raised
on rice and engines.

11:44.578 --> 11:47.373
Why don't you avoid

11:47.456 --> 11:50.292
talking about rice today?

11:53.212 --> 11:54.839
Did you two plan something?

11:56.715 --> 11:58.092
You clearly know each other.

12:04.306 --> 12:06.058
You said you'd stay hidden.

12:06.142 --> 12:08.352
How can you get caught
in less than 12 hours?

12:08.436 --> 12:10.938
Don't worry. I have a plan.

12:13.149 --> 12:14.692
I need a change in direction.

12:15.276 --> 12:17.570
Half a day in, and you're doing this here?

12:18.070 --> 12:22.324
Why did Ki Ka-young die for them
when she had no interest in dying for me?

12:22.825 --> 12:24.452
What makes me different from them?

12:25.828 --> 12:27.163
I should've checked that.

12:28.372 --> 12:29.290
I'll be back.

12:31.750 --> 12:33.419
Where are you off to now?

12:34.128 --> 12:36.130
[dramatic music playing]

12:37.298 --> 12:38.132
Comrades.

12:38.215 --> 12:39.258
OCTOBER, 1909
PRIMORSKY KRAI

12:39.341 --> 12:41.677
Let us meet again
at Harbin Station. Alive.

12:42.428 --> 12:43.262
Yes.

12:48.184 --> 12:49.143
[Iblis] Ki Ka-young?

12:50.769 --> 12:51.770
Oh. Ah.

12:52.480 --> 12:53.314
Who are you?

12:53.397 --> 12:54.773
Hi, past-life Ki Ka-young.

12:54.857 --> 12:56.525
I need to ask you something.

12:58.444 --> 12:59.445
Know of An Jung-geun?

13:00.738 --> 13:01.572
Comrades!

13:01.655 --> 13:05.534
Our location has been compromised!
Run, now! Hurry! [panting]

13:07.036 --> 13:08.329
So you are a spy.

13:08.412 --> 13:09.371
A spy?

13:10.039 --> 13:10.873
What's that?

13:11.749 --> 13:14.126
-No, I just have a question.
-[hurried footsteps approaching]

13:14.210 --> 13:15.961
[amusing music playing]

13:16.045 --> 13:17.630
-[soldier] Fire!
-[man] Run!

13:19.256 --> 13:20.966
So loud. No, stop!

13:24.720 --> 13:26.597
Come on, that stings!

13:27.640 --> 13:29.308
Hey! We were talking over here!

13:29.391 --> 13:30.851
What do you keep throwing at me?

13:33.187 --> 13:35.940
[all grunting, groaning]

13:36.023 --> 13:37.733
-[gasps]
-[all groaning]

13:38.400 --> 13:41.570
I was only trying to return them to you.
Right, Ki Ka-young.

13:42.655 --> 13:44.907
Where are you going? Wait for me!

13:45.407 --> 13:48.661
I said I have a question.
I swear it won't take long! [pants]

13:50.246 --> 13:51.247
Thanks for saving me.

13:52.581 --> 13:54.375
If we are granted another life,

13:55.584 --> 13:56.710
I hope we meet again.

13:57.211 --> 13:59.547
Wait, no.
I want to talk to you in this life…

13:59.630 --> 14:01.340
Get him first!

14:01.423 --> 14:02.675
Fire!

14:02.758 --> 14:03.884
That stings!

14:03.968 --> 14:05.970
Stop giving me these things!

14:06.053 --> 14:08.430
-[all grunt, groan]
-[gasps]

14:08.514 --> 14:10.140
-There he is!
-Right, Ki Ka-young.

14:10.224 --> 14:11.350
Wait, I…

14:11.892 --> 14:13.561
[sighs] This life just won't do.

14:18.899 --> 14:22.027
THE YEAR 1592

14:23.362 --> 14:24.905
[dramatic music playing]

14:27.950 --> 14:29.618
[horse whinnies]

14:30.911 --> 14:33.372
[Chang-sik] A messenger is here
from Jeolla's naval command.

14:33.455 --> 14:34.290
[king] Let him in.

14:38.377 --> 14:40.504
-You may approach.
-Yes, sir.

14:45.926 --> 14:47.011
[Iblis] Ki Ka-young.

14:54.435 --> 14:55.269
Ki Ka-young.

14:56.228 --> 14:58.898
-[man 1] What was that?
-[man 2] What was that sound just now?

14:58.981 --> 14:59.899
You're a man now?

15:01.525 --> 15:02.359
[Ka-young gasps]

15:02.443 --> 15:04.320
[comical music playing]

15:10.242 --> 15:12.745
Ki Ka-young. I have a question for you.

15:12.828 --> 15:13.704
[Chang-sik] Your Majesty.

15:13.787 --> 15:17.166
I, Yi Sun-sin, Left Naval Commander
of Jeolla Province, humbly report.

15:17.249 --> 15:20.127
Yes. It's about that man, Yi Sun-sin.

15:20.210 --> 15:23.464
Our forces struck Busan Port's
enemy base, sinking 130 ships…

15:23.547 --> 15:24.757
-Ki Ka-young.
-Ki Ka-young.

15:26.467 --> 15:28.844
-No, kicking, no, killing…
-Huh?

15:28.928 --> 15:30.429
Command my death, Your Majesty.

15:30.930 --> 15:33.390
[king] Who was that? Come on out.

15:34.350 --> 15:36.852
Who keeps going on about "Ki Ka-young"?

15:40.981 --> 15:41.941
[Iblis] Oh.

15:42.566 --> 15:44.735
-Ah.
-[man 1] Goodness, how can this be?

15:44.818 --> 15:45.778
[man 2] What is that?

15:45.861 --> 15:46.820
[gasps]

15:47.404 --> 15:48.530
[man 3] Who is that?

15:48.614 --> 15:49.990
[man 4] Is he a person or a ghost?

15:50.074 --> 15:52.409
I have a pressing question, you see.
[chuckles]

15:53.619 --> 15:55.663
That peculiar, freakish…

15:56.664 --> 15:59.458
Seize that monstrous being
and decapitate it at once!

16:00.668 --> 16:01.669
Decapitate?

16:03.545 --> 16:04.546
What does that mean?

16:06.340 --> 16:09.635
[radio narrator] And so, it was recorded
in one unofficial Joseon text

16:09.718 --> 16:13.722
that the being stayed alive
for three days even after being beheaded

16:13.806 --> 16:17.142
and, for all three days,
continued its bizarre cries,

16:17.226 --> 16:22.815
saying "Kay Young, Kay Young"
before vanishing into thin air.

16:23.357 --> 16:25.025
[mystical music playing on radio]

16:25.609 --> 16:26.610
Where have you been?

16:26.694 --> 16:29.279
Far away. [chuckles softly]

16:30.781 --> 16:32.116
-[neck cracks]
-[groans]

16:37.579 --> 16:39.957
There were some people
I needed to meet up with.

16:40.791 --> 16:43.252
What the hell are you playing at?

16:43.752 --> 16:46.588
I made a wish like you wanted.
Why aren't you doing any work?

16:47.256 --> 16:49.425
You're just stalling for time, aren't you?

16:50.050 --> 16:50.926
Not at all!

16:51.510 --> 16:55.597
I've arranged it so that the lamp
will show itself when their desire peaks.

16:58.183 --> 17:01.812
But if someone's wish changes things,
how would I know?

17:01.895 --> 17:02.771
What about that?

17:08.861 --> 17:10.404
Once you write with this pen,

17:10.487 --> 17:13.532
your words are eternally binding,
no matter how things may change?

17:14.158 --> 17:16.702
And we're here to get it?
At the crack of dawn?

17:16.785 --> 17:18.328
[Iblis] Yes. It'll be right here.

17:19.496 --> 17:21.081
But the process is complicated,

17:22.666 --> 17:24.251
and I'll need your help.

17:24.835 --> 17:27.046
[door opens, closes]

17:29.590 --> 17:30.549
[suspenseful music playing]

17:30.632 --> 17:31.467
[sighs]

17:32.468 --> 17:35.262
He owns this building.
Did you get permission to be up here?

17:35.345 --> 17:37.890
Between us,
permission will never be necessary.

17:39.391 --> 17:41.226
Pluck a feather while he's distracted.

17:42.644 --> 17:43.771
Then run.

17:45.731 --> 17:46.565
What?

17:47.816 --> 17:48.942
Whoa!

17:49.985 --> 17:50.944
Why, you…

17:51.820 --> 17:53.906
-[laughing]
-[Ka-young screaming]

17:53.989 --> 17:57.785
-[gasps, screams]
-[Ka-young] This is so much fun!

17:57.868 --> 18:00.329
[man screams] I got you! [pants]

18:00.412 --> 18:02.081
[screaming]

18:09.004 --> 18:11.131
[both screaming]

18:12.424 --> 18:13.717
[man panting]

18:17.429 --> 18:18.263
Are you okay?

18:18.931 --> 18:20.140
Yes, well, I'm fine.

18:21.350 --> 18:24.228
Why were you screaming
when you have wings?

18:24.311 --> 18:26.480
I was just nervous
since it's been a while.

18:27.106 --> 18:28.649
Is your auto shop doing well?

18:28.732 --> 18:29.900
You could say that.

18:31.360 --> 18:33.612
Anyway, you'll feel a pinch.

18:34.154 --> 18:35.614
[yelps]

18:36.490 --> 18:38.742
Damn it!
I'm already stressed from molting.

18:39.368 --> 18:41.328
Hey! How many did you pluck?

18:43.080 --> 18:45.624
-[sighs]
-[Iblis] Long time no see, brother.

18:47.042 --> 18:49.378
I heard you got out, brother.

18:49.461 --> 18:51.171
It's been, what, almost 1,000 years?

18:51.255 --> 18:55.217
So, in my absence,
was the world full of peace and quiet?

18:55.759 --> 18:59.388
You condemned me,
saying I led humans astray. [scoffs]

18:59.471 --> 19:02.683
So tell me. In a world without me,
were all humans kind?

19:02.766 --> 19:07.062
I've seen that war, murder, greed,
and selfishness all continued to exist,

19:08.021 --> 19:09.148
even in my absence.

19:09.231 --> 19:11.316
Ever think they're the seeds you sowed?

19:11.900 --> 19:15.445
The idea of humans getting a chance
to make a wish is just wrong.

19:16.280 --> 19:18.407
-Hasn't it ever occurred to you?
-No, it hasn't.

19:18.490 --> 19:19.658
All that occurs to me

19:19.741 --> 19:22.536
is how those flawed lumps of clay
are his mistake.

19:22.619 --> 19:25.164
Proving that hell is fitting
for those lumps of clay

19:25.831 --> 19:27.791
is the task that he bestowed upon me.

19:27.875 --> 19:30.377
Don't forget that
he also bestowed me with a task.

19:30.878 --> 19:34.089
I'm pretty sure you took from my wing
before you were locked up.

19:34.173 --> 19:35.674
What are you up to this time?

19:35.757 --> 19:36.884
Never you mind.

19:37.384 --> 19:38.927
While I was locked up,

19:39.011 --> 19:42.306
for 983 years
without skipping a single day,

19:43.348 --> 19:45.726
you came to visit the desert
where I was locked up

19:46.351 --> 19:48.854
and poured a handful of sand over my lamp.

19:49.605 --> 19:50.689
Was it heavy?

19:51.273 --> 19:54.151
You ought to experience
the burdens humans live with.

19:54.234 --> 19:57.654
[laughs] My goodness.
You really are an angel, aren't you?

20:00.115 --> 20:02.367
Enough chitchat. Let's truly catch up.

20:02.868 --> 20:05.412
If you wish.
Though, this will be the last time.

20:06.997 --> 20:08.665
I'll be coming for your throat soon.

20:09.875 --> 20:10.918
[mockingly] Ah.

20:18.592 --> 20:19.426
[laughs]

20:19.509 --> 20:21.261
[panting]

20:22.971 --> 20:24.431
Wait, where did he go?

20:24.514 --> 20:26.516
[whistling]

20:28.644 --> 20:29.686
[stops whistling]

20:40.781 --> 20:43.283
[upbeat music playing]

20:51.124 --> 20:52.793
-Oh!
-[rumbling]

20:55.128 --> 20:56.296
Hey! Damn you!

20:57.464 --> 20:58.966
[exhales] Phew.

20:59.758 --> 21:02.094
Are you nuts?
Did you just bust through my building?

21:02.594 --> 21:05.514
All the units are sold,
and everyone's due to move in next week!

21:05.597 --> 21:06.723
[laughs]

21:06.807 --> 21:08.642
Any idea what this building's worth?

21:08.725 --> 21:09.643
Let's see.

21:10.185 --> 21:12.980
Would it be worth
the weight of your hypocrisy?

21:13.063 --> 21:13.981
Why, you little!

21:14.064 --> 21:14.898
[giggles]

21:14.982 --> 21:17.693
For a second there,
I almost forgot you were Satan.

21:18.819 --> 21:20.195
Is it hitting home now?

21:22.614 --> 21:24.408
You better watch your back,

21:25.075 --> 21:26.952
for I have returned, brother.

21:29.037 --> 21:29.997
[laughs]

21:31.206 --> 21:34.543
That damn little… [breathing heavily]

21:35.210 --> 21:38.171
[yells in frustration, grunts]

21:52.311 --> 21:54.229
It can only write truths?

22:00.986 --> 22:04.489
WRITTEN BY KI KA-YOUNG

22:04.573 --> 22:08.744
A NEGATIVE ONE AND A STONE IN A SHOE

22:15.292 --> 22:19.212
GENIE HAS GOOD LOOKS

22:20.922 --> 22:21.757
It works.

22:22.799 --> 22:24.051
GENIE HAS LOOKS

22:24.634 --> 22:26.803
Wow. Brutal.

22:30.599 --> 22:34.436
I AM

22:37.647 --> 22:40.400
I AM GRANDMA'S BURDEN

22:44.112 --> 22:45.697
I AM GRANDMA'S STRENGTH

22:45.781 --> 22:47.783
[gentle music playing]

22:54.122 --> 22:55.540
Ka-young.

22:56.041 --> 22:57.209
Try some of these.

22:57.834 --> 23:01.880
Chang-sik dropped off a huge basketful,
and they're incredibly sweet.

23:04.841 --> 23:06.510
-Grandma.
-Yes?

23:08.178 --> 23:10.347
All this time,
I've been fooled by everyone.

23:10.847 --> 23:12.974
I'm not a burden to you, Grandma.

23:13.892 --> 23:14.810
I'm your strength.

23:14.893 --> 23:15.936
Goodness me.

23:16.019 --> 23:19.147
You must not be all that smart
if you're only just figuring that out.

23:19.231 --> 23:21.024
I guess being first doesn't mean much.

23:21.108 --> 23:24.111
[laughs] Eat up. It'll give you strength.

23:24.694 --> 23:25.946
[chuckles]

23:26.655 --> 23:31.576
Actually, Grandma,
strawberries have vitamin C, not strength.

23:31.660 --> 23:35.539
For strength, you want to consume
a primary energy source, like carbs…

23:35.622 --> 23:36.456
Grandma?

23:36.957 --> 23:38.959
[dreamy music playing]

23:44.172 --> 23:46.341
[grunts, exclaims]

23:49.219 --> 23:52.180
Seriously, what's going on
in that head of yours?

23:52.264 --> 23:53.765
Aren't you going to do any work?

23:54.599 --> 23:57.018
-Gonna sell the strawberries next year?
-Aye, ma'am!

23:57.519 --> 23:58.395
It's no big deal.

23:59.271 --> 24:00.272
It wasn't mutual.

24:01.648 --> 24:02.774
It was one-sided.

24:03.400 --> 24:04.276
By the way,

24:04.359 --> 24:08.071
I heard that men in the Middle East
really do rub noses like that.

24:08.155 --> 24:11.867
I hear they only do that to dignitaries
whom they deeply respect.

24:11.950 --> 24:13.618
What, so I'm a dignitary?

24:13.702 --> 24:15.912
-I guess so.
-[laughing]

24:23.837 --> 24:25.255
You're the only one for me!

24:25.338 --> 24:28.300
Peace has been restored
to our briefly rattled family!

24:28.383 --> 24:29.968
-[laughing]
-Sure, all right.

24:30.886 --> 24:34.222
What kind of fresh bullcrap is this?
[laughs]

24:34.306 --> 24:37.225
Didn't you say there was a draw
to assign festival booths?

24:37.309 --> 24:39.477
-Get to work, will you?
-Aye, ma'am!

24:40.395 --> 24:44.065
Please do your best to keep sales steady
during the festival period.

24:44.149 --> 24:45.859
Our branch manager is very concerned.

24:45.942 --> 24:49.404
Pay closer attention to the displays
and offer samples proactively.

24:49.487 --> 24:51.281
Yes, ma'am.

24:51.364 --> 24:52.991
[sighs] Kang Im-seon?

24:53.783 --> 24:55.869
I've told you multiple times
to wear makeup.

24:56.369 --> 24:58.079
And remove that pain relief patch.

25:01.166 --> 25:02.083
Hello?

25:02.167 --> 25:03.793
Answer me, please.

25:03.877 --> 25:05.545
Yes, Assistant Manager Lee.

25:11.092 --> 25:13.470
Ow. [wincing]

25:17.307 --> 25:18.141
[grunts softly]

25:22.103 --> 25:22.938
Huh?

25:23.605 --> 25:24.981
What's this?

25:26.566 --> 25:28.526
I didn't know we sold anything like this.

25:30.403 --> 25:31.571
[blows]

25:31.655 --> 25:32.530
[groans]

25:33.114 --> 25:34.199
Come on.

25:35.408 --> 25:40.705
-[enchanting music playing]
-[chiming softly]

25:50.257 --> 25:51.716
-[whooshes]
-[yelps]

25:58.473 --> 25:59.474
What is that?

26:00.517 --> 26:02.852
I am Genie, the lamp spirit.

26:03.979 --> 26:05.855
I shall grant you three wishes.

26:08.858 --> 26:09.693
Make them.

26:11.861 --> 26:13.405
No bringing back the dead.

26:14.322 --> 26:15.573
No traveling to the future.

26:16.324 --> 26:19.828
Anything besides that, your wish…

26:22.247 --> 26:23.456
is my command.

26:25.709 --> 26:27.794
[breath trembling]

26:32.966 --> 26:34.509
She made her first wish?

26:37.554 --> 26:40.098
Hmm. I get what the negative one means,

26:41.725 --> 26:43.184
but what's with the stone?

26:44.227 --> 26:46.479
-There's always something.
-Not your concern.

26:47.522 --> 26:49.524
So what did Ms. Kang wish for?

26:51.484 --> 26:52.444
[chuckles]

26:52.527 --> 26:54.070
[dramatic music playing]

26:55.989 --> 27:00.910
KANG IM-SEON, SUPERMARKET EMPLOYEE

27:00.994 --> 27:07.625
APRIL 19, 2024, MADE HER FIRST WISH

27:07.709 --> 27:11.671
I'm Kang Im-seon,
your newly appointed branch manager.

27:11.755 --> 27:14.883
TO BECOME BRANCH MANAGER

27:15.633 --> 27:18.470
I've worked
at this supermarket for 20 years,

27:19.054 --> 27:21.222
since the year after it opened.

27:21.806 --> 27:22.807
But that young brat

27:22.891 --> 27:25.769
landed assistant manager
just by having a college degree.

27:26.811 --> 27:28.355
I'm still just a temp.

27:30.899 --> 27:33.318
Make me that bitch's superior officer.

27:33.902 --> 27:35.028
The branch manager.

27:37.405 --> 27:38.990
That is my first wish.

27:39.074 --> 27:40.492
[music intensifies]

27:44.954 --> 27:47.665
Oh boy. Good for you, Im-seon.

27:48.249 --> 27:50.001
She worked so hard.

27:50.502 --> 27:51.836
Congratulations.

27:54.506 --> 27:55.590
Assistant Manager Lee?

27:56.091 --> 27:58.426
You'll work the frozen goods
discount display today.

27:59.010 --> 28:00.345
-Me?
-Mmm.

28:00.428 --> 28:02.764
You never seem satisfied
with the employees' work.

28:02.847 --> 28:05.350
And wear a lighter shade of lipstick.

28:05.433 --> 28:07.894
Stop wafting your perfume
around the tasting stations.

28:10.355 --> 28:11.231
Hello?

28:13.233 --> 28:14.234
Answer me, please!

28:16.444 --> 28:18.405
Yes, Branch Manager Kang.

28:20.865 --> 28:24.160
Hmm. All right, then.
Let's open our doors.

28:24.661 --> 28:25.870
[employees] Yes, ma'am.

28:27.622 --> 28:29.499
What on earth is going on?

28:29.999 --> 28:33.753
I know. How can a temp employee
become branch manager overnight?

28:34.254 --> 28:35.380
How did that happen?

28:35.964 --> 28:36.965
[woman] Who knows?

28:38.174 --> 28:41.052
Ah. You're due for an oil change.

28:41.636 --> 28:43.388
I am, aren't I?

28:44.806 --> 28:45.765
Actually,

28:46.516 --> 28:47.976
I'll be getting a new car.

28:48.601 --> 28:49.477
An imported one.

28:49.561 --> 28:51.479
Don't you worry about me anymore.

28:56.943 --> 28:58.319
Are you seeing it now?

28:58.945 --> 29:00.530
The true nature of humanity?

29:01.364 --> 29:03.116
One thing I definitely didn't know.

29:03.825 --> 29:04.993
That I'd lose a client.

29:06.244 --> 29:08.913
But is it okay for you
to be seen with me like this?

29:08.997 --> 29:12.959
The wishmakers know you're a genie.
Shouldn't you avoid being seen with me?

29:13.042 --> 29:13.960
Ha.

29:14.878 --> 29:17.213
In their eyes, I'm a mere sand whirl.

29:18.214 --> 29:21.009
But I tend to emit a golden light
to appear more mystical.

29:21.509 --> 29:24.220
There's no real functional purpose.
[chuckles]

29:26.306 --> 29:29.184
Min-ji tends to wear a gown
to appear more like a dentist.

29:29.267 --> 29:30.435
Oh!

29:30.518 --> 29:32.937
If one holds a syringe without a gown on…

29:34.439 --> 29:35.273
Um…

29:37.400 --> 29:39.152
You're really gonna cut it off there?

29:39.652 --> 29:41.404
Wow. You're evil.

29:44.449 --> 29:47.952
I've been itching to know for ages.
Who even is this Min-ji?

29:49.996 --> 29:52.207
[girl 1] Would you move
your damn head, Choi Min-ji?

29:52.290 --> 29:55.084
I can't see the psychopath's head
because of you.

29:57.921 --> 30:00.799
So, do you really have the urge
to kill people and stuff?

30:01.925 --> 30:03.301
In gruesome ways?

30:05.970 --> 30:07.096
I did just now.

30:07.180 --> 30:08.264
-Just now?
-[girls laugh]

30:09.098 --> 30:11.226
Damn, I almost pissed myself.

30:11.810 --> 30:12.811
Getting hit hurts.

30:12.894 --> 30:15.230
She might not say it,
but it still physically hurts.

30:15.313 --> 30:17.023
-Did she fucking say "physically"?
-[girls laugh]

30:17.732 --> 30:20.902
That's why we hit her, dumbass.
So it hurts.

30:24.405 --> 30:26.157
[Ka-young] You do that
even though you know?

30:26.741 --> 30:28.701
You know the rules, yet you still hit her?

30:29.327 --> 30:30.495
You don't hold back?

30:31.287 --> 30:33.498
-[suspenseful music playing]
-[girls giggling]

30:34.833 --> 30:36.125
[girl 1] This is fucking boring.

30:36.209 --> 30:38.837
Hey, let's finish this smoke and bounce.

30:38.920 --> 30:40.922
[suspenseful music continues]

30:44.133 --> 30:45.969
[watch ticking]

30:46.719 --> 30:47.554
[door unlocks, opens]

30:49.556 --> 30:52.016
Ugh. What the fuck? I smell gasoline.

30:52.600 --> 30:54.310
It fucking reeks of gasoline.

30:54.394 --> 30:56.604
You fucking bitch.
What the hell are you doing?

30:56.688 --> 30:58.022
Setting this place on fire.

30:58.106 --> 31:00.483
The story will be
you started the fire while smoking.

31:00.567 --> 31:02.819
Do we look like dipshits to you,
you psycho bitch?

31:02.902 --> 31:04.279
There are so many witnesses--

31:04.362 --> 31:06.114
-Fuck!
-Damn it!

31:07.115 --> 31:07.949
So?

31:08.533 --> 31:10.743
Shall I eliminate the witnesses, then?

31:11.369 --> 31:12.370
[girls yelp]

31:12.453 --> 31:14.914
Okay, we get it. Fine. We won't touch you.

31:14.998 --> 31:18.543
Don't touch Choi Min-ji either.
This is our new rule.

31:19.460 --> 31:20.420
Fine.

31:26.175 --> 31:27.093
Be my friend.

31:27.176 --> 31:29.178
We're the only ones
who don't have friends.

31:29.888 --> 31:33.224
In South Korea, it's far more efficient
to be in a pair than alone.

31:34.017 --> 31:36.102
What happens if I say I don't want to?

31:36.185 --> 31:37.604
You don't have a choice.

31:37.687 --> 31:40.148
That's why, starting today,
you and I are friends.

31:41.024 --> 31:42.609
Also, your grades suck.

31:43.443 --> 31:44.527
Memorize all of this.

31:44.611 --> 31:46.112
If you don't, I'll kill you.

31:47.780 --> 31:49.949
Solve these, or I'll kill you.

31:52.118 --> 31:54.370
Pass the interview and oral exam.

31:54.454 --> 31:56.122
If you don't, I'll kill you.

31:56.205 --> 31:57.832
That's what I needed to hear.

31:58.416 --> 31:59.918
You have no other choice.

32:00.835 --> 32:02.128
Pass, Choi Min-ji!

32:02.211 --> 32:05.006
ODD TEETH AND ODD PEOPLE WELCOME

32:05.089 --> 32:07.550
That's so funny.
It says, "Odd people welcome."

32:07.634 --> 32:09.636
-How ridiculous.
-Tell me about it.

32:09.719 --> 32:13.431
In my experience,
it's the odd ones who change the world.

32:14.223 --> 32:17.018
One of the wishmakers
from Ms. Ki Ka-young's first wish

32:17.101 --> 32:18.811
has made their first wish.

32:18.895 --> 32:21.481
Today's Cheongpung
is not the same as yesterday's.

32:21.564 --> 32:23.733
[squeals] Congratulations, Master.

32:24.651 --> 32:27.612
If we steer Ms. Ki Ka-young's
last two wishes the right way,

32:27.695 --> 32:30.907
you'll at last be able to do
what you've longed for.

32:30.990 --> 32:32.200
Slit Iblis's throat.

32:32.283 --> 32:34.410
So that's what they wanted my wing for.

32:34.494 --> 32:35.370
To keep a record.

32:36.037 --> 32:37.038
Hmm.

32:37.538 --> 32:40.833
You know it took me 20 years
to study psychopaths, don't you?

32:41.417 --> 32:44.420
I actually thought Ki Ka-young
wouldn't make any wishes.

32:44.504 --> 32:48.716
For now, I'm happy that I've caught
a lucky break, but something feels off.

32:49.592 --> 32:52.804
I tossed all my books, but maybe
I'm not done researching psychopaths.

32:53.763 --> 32:55.723
Anyway, what's Iblis up to these days?

32:55.807 --> 32:57.558
Canned beer and video game machines.

32:59.602 --> 33:01.813
-Think he'll show up when he's broke?
-Yes.

33:02.313 --> 33:04.065
He's using Sade's money right now.

33:04.565 --> 33:07.902
Hate comments have been flooding
the foundation's website since yesterday.

33:08.403 --> 33:10.947
Judging by the typos and content,
they're clearly written

33:11.781 --> 33:12.949
by Iblis.

33:13.032 --> 33:14.575
BEAUTIFUL RYU SU-HYEON. RESPECT!

33:14.659 --> 33:15.952
ANON: WHY? ARE YOU STOOPID?

33:16.035 --> 33:17.954
[grunting in frustration]

33:20.289 --> 33:23.918
-[indistinct chatter on video game]
-[yelping]

33:24.877 --> 33:26.129
Huh?

33:27.130 --> 33:28.423
No!

33:29.298 --> 33:31.009
-Please, no!
-[clattering]

33:32.802 --> 33:35.722
Oh? Sang-hyeok found money
when he did this.

33:40.101 --> 33:41.436
[game announcer in English] Game over!

33:44.480 --> 33:46.566
[amusing music playing]

33:46.649 --> 33:47.608
Hey, human.

33:51.112 --> 33:53.322
Who? Me?

33:57.452 --> 33:58.286
What do you want?

33:59.162 --> 34:00.079
Pick it up.

34:00.163 --> 34:01.873
The Earth is hurting.

34:01.956 --> 34:04.083
Even Ki Ka-young picks up after herself.

34:04.834 --> 34:06.377
-[scoffs]
-The Earth?

34:07.170 --> 34:08.921
Ah! It's hurting?

34:09.714 --> 34:12.091
Ah, I guess today's my lucky day.

34:19.974 --> 34:22.351
I'm gonna toss this one too.
Infuriating, isn't it?

34:22.435 --> 34:23.561
Then hit me.

34:23.644 --> 34:24.854
Wow.

34:25.938 --> 34:26.898
I almost swooned.

34:27.565 --> 34:28.441
Ah.

34:29.150 --> 34:31.527
Any other day, you'd be exactly my type,

34:32.028 --> 34:33.112
but not today.

34:33.196 --> 34:37.742
-Sade!
-[whooshes]

34:39.077 --> 34:40.953
[suspenseful music playing]

34:41.037 --> 34:41.913
Yes, Master.

34:41.996 --> 34:45.208
What the heck? Where'd you show up from?

34:45.291 --> 34:46.709
Take care of him for me.

34:47.293 --> 34:49.128
And hand over any spare change you have.

34:50.296 --> 34:52.048
[coins jingling]

34:52.131 --> 34:53.758
That was incredibly smooth.

34:56.094 --> 34:57.595
Keep glaring at me. I dare you.

34:59.472 --> 35:00.473
[laughs]

35:03.142 --> 35:06.687
Come on, bring it. Just so you know,
touch me, and I'll demand a settlement.

35:06.771 --> 35:07.647
Got it?

35:08.564 --> 35:09.482
[grunts softly]

35:10.900 --> 35:12.193
-[growls]
-[man screaming]

35:12.276 --> 35:15.071
Don't come any closer! [screaming]

35:17.907 --> 35:19.617
Back off! Don't come any closer!

35:20.118 --> 35:22.829
[Sade] What are you going to do
about the 1,800 won I lost because of you?

35:22.912 --> 35:24.163
[growling]

35:25.373 --> 35:26.207
[owl hoots]

35:26.290 --> 35:27.458
[Irem] Nice going.

35:27.542 --> 35:28.501
[Sade] Irem!

35:29.001 --> 35:30.044
[hoots]

35:30.128 --> 35:33.214
[Sade] How long has it been? 100 years?

35:34.298 --> 35:37.093
Excuse me. Have you seen a girl
who looks like this?

35:38.094 --> 35:39.929
[hooting]

35:40.596 --> 35:42.932
[gasps] Ah.

35:43.015 --> 35:45.184
-[hoots]
-Irem!

35:46.602 --> 35:50.606
[Sade] So you've been here
the whole time since then?

35:50.690 --> 35:53.192
[Irem] Yes. Ejllael decided
to settle here.

35:53.276 --> 35:55.653
Death ran rampant back then.

35:57.530 --> 35:59.490
[Jong-heon] They said it was black,
so keep an eye out.

35:59.574 --> 36:00.449
[Chang-sik] Okay.

36:00.533 --> 36:02.285
[Min-jae] Shouldn't we search
during the day?

36:06.455 --> 36:08.124
Who goes there? Who are you?

36:08.666 --> 36:11.002
Is that Director Ryu's assistant
and Mr. Seo I-deuk?

36:11.085 --> 36:13.671
This isn't the time or place
for a rendezvous.

36:13.754 --> 36:17.091
A panther or whatever was spotted
in town, and everyone's on edge.

36:17.175 --> 36:19.677
Are you sure
it's a panther and not a jaguar-- [grunts]

36:20.386 --> 36:21.262
A jaguar?

36:21.345 --> 36:24.599
It's probably hiding in the mountains,
so let's head back down now.

36:24.682 --> 36:26.392
-It's dangerous. Go on.
-Sure, thanks.

36:26.475 --> 36:27.393
[Chang-sik] Hurry along.

36:27.977 --> 36:29.061
Goodbye.

36:29.145 --> 36:30.605
-Go.
-[Irem chuckles]

36:30.688 --> 36:31.689
Hold on a second.

36:34.025 --> 36:34.859
That tail…

36:36.027 --> 36:36.944
Huh?

36:37.653 --> 36:38.487
And those ears.

36:42.325 --> 36:44.076
We went to Everland today.

36:44.160 --> 36:46.162
They're hot off the shelf.
Aren't they cute?

36:46.245 --> 36:50.541
[chuckles] Is that right? I must say,
they're so realistic. Go on.

36:51.292 --> 36:52.126
Hurry along.

36:53.336 --> 36:55.588
[squeaking]

36:55.671 --> 36:57.715
Grr… Roar.

36:58.424 --> 37:00.343
Shall we hear about
what happened overnight?

37:00.426 --> 37:02.178
[brown mouse] I would rather die
an honorable death

37:02.261 --> 37:03.346
than submit to my mortal enemy.

37:03.429 --> 37:06.474
[laughs] This is a bad look for jaguars.

37:07.058 --> 37:08.684
[growls] I'll bite you.

37:08.768 --> 37:12.647
[white mouse] Please. My elderly mother
is waiting for me at home.

37:12.730 --> 37:13.564
Then

37:14.232 --> 37:16.359
why are you out so late?

37:16.984 --> 37:18.110
You're excused. Go.

37:19.737 --> 37:21.405
-[squeaks]
-[growls softly]

37:22.406 --> 37:24.283
Still want to die an honorable death?

37:24.367 --> 37:27.453
-[squeaking]
-[growling softly]

37:29.247 --> 37:31.874
I did some digging as you ordered me to.

37:31.958 --> 37:35.419
The auto shop is her side hustle,
and she actually has another day job.

37:36.128 --> 37:36.963
[key clacks]

37:38.256 --> 37:39.090
Ah.

37:39.715 --> 37:41.008
Elon Musk.

37:41.592 --> 37:43.344
Should I just kill him? [slams table]

37:51.394 --> 37:53.145
[groans, sighs]

37:53.229 --> 37:56.315
She must have made a fortune.
She didn't even pick up the pen.

37:56.899 --> 37:59.527
And now comes the really important intel.

38:00.194 --> 38:01.028
Go on.

38:01.654 --> 38:04.407
How come you close shop
every 4th, 14th, and 24th?

38:04.490 --> 38:06.826
Any particular reason, boss?

38:08.953 --> 38:09.912
Four. Death's number.

38:09.996 --> 38:10.871
DEATH

38:10.955 --> 38:11.789
Hmm?

38:12.623 --> 38:14.875
-She wants Death's number?
-No, that's not it.

38:14.959 --> 38:19.505
Anyway, rain or shine,
she has a routine that she sticks to.

38:20.006 --> 38:22.508
Scuba diving on the 4th.
Hiking on the 14th.

38:22.591 --> 38:24.010
The workshop on the 24th.

38:24.093 --> 38:25.720
-And every Wednesday--
-Gamja-tang!

38:25.803 --> 38:26.637
Ah.

38:27.513 --> 38:28.347
Wow.

38:30.599 --> 38:32.351
So that's what that meant.

38:32.852 --> 38:34.854
[gentle music playing]

38:46.657 --> 38:48.617
[Iblis] "As natural a death as possible."

38:50.077 --> 38:52.246
"…like deep-sea equipment failure…

38:52.830 --> 38:55.541
[breathing heavily]

38:55.624 --> 38:57.877
or a fall on a remote trail."

38:57.960 --> 38:58.961
[exclaims softly]

39:00.671 --> 39:01.505
[sighs]

39:02.131 --> 39:03.924
[machine whirring]

39:09.680 --> 39:11.724
[Iblis] Ki Ka-young's entire routine

39:11.807 --> 39:14.477
is her way of preparing for her death.

39:15.227 --> 39:17.313
The fact that a human body is 70% water

39:17.396 --> 39:19.774
means that blood
is the heaviest part of it.

39:20.399 --> 39:23.736
So I thought about it, and if you start
by draining the blood, and then…

39:24.487 --> 39:27.406
Here, here, here,

39:28.324 --> 39:29.241
and here.

39:30.117 --> 39:32.370
If you chop them up like so
and stack the pieces,

39:32.870 --> 39:34.038
you'd only need a coffin…

39:36.290 --> 39:37.666
about this small, no?

39:37.750 --> 39:41.003
Ms. Ki Ka-young.
I'm moving overseas next week.

39:42.004 --> 39:43.631
Is business here that slow?

39:52.515 --> 39:54.809
So she just bought the place.

40:01.065 --> 40:01.982
Wow.

40:02.900 --> 40:03.734
Coffins and all?

40:04.777 --> 40:05.611
[sighs]

40:05.694 --> 40:07.822
She plans to die
as soon as Oh Pan-geum does.

40:07.905 --> 40:09.115
What if she dies too soon?

40:09.198 --> 40:11.325
You can't exactly
take revenge on the dead.

40:11.409 --> 40:13.536
We'll just have to stop her
from dying too soon.

40:14.161 --> 40:15.454
I have my ways.

40:17.081 --> 40:17.915
Let's make sure

40:19.500 --> 40:21.043
Oh Pan-geum sticks around.

40:24.797 --> 40:28.092
Oh dear, my back. My goodness.

40:29.176 --> 40:32.054
I'm so old. I should just die soon.

40:32.555 --> 40:33.556
-No!
-Good heavens!

40:33.639 --> 40:34.765
Where on your back?

40:35.683 --> 40:37.393
-Where does it hurt? Lie down.
-Oh!

40:38.060 --> 40:40.229
Is it here? Or here? Or maybe here?

40:40.312 --> 40:41.522
-What are you doing?
-Here?

40:41.605 --> 40:43.649
How's that?
Think you'll live a little longer?

40:43.732 --> 40:45.734
[comical music playing]

40:46.485 --> 40:48.362
Good heavens, my shoulder.

40:48.946 --> 40:52.324
What would be the use in cooking
a delicious stew with this garlic?

40:52.408 --> 40:53.325
In my old age--

40:53.409 --> 40:54.493
[Iblis] No!

40:54.577 --> 40:55.744
What about the garlic?

40:56.495 --> 40:58.414
Should I grind it? Hand it here.

41:02.084 --> 41:05.921
If you followed her here
all the way from the Middle East,

41:06.005 --> 41:08.007
you must have
some pretty serious feelings.

41:08.090 --> 41:10.176
Well, I knew as soon as I saw her

41:10.259 --> 41:12.803
that she was the one
I'd been waiting for all this time.

41:12.887 --> 41:13.762
Goodness me.

41:14.555 --> 41:16.432
At first sight? Right away?

41:17.391 --> 41:19.643
Of course, Ki Ka-young
didn't believe me at first.

41:21.896 --> 41:24.356
So I took her up a skyscraper.

41:24.440 --> 41:27.610
One of those places where you can see
all the city lights and the night sky?

41:27.693 --> 41:31.614
-Mmm.
-So what did you do up there?

41:33.407 --> 41:35.367
That's a little intense for your ears.

41:36.410 --> 41:37.745
But one thing's for sure.

41:37.828 --> 41:40.873
Ki Ka-young is unlike
any other woman I've ever met.

41:40.956 --> 41:43.167
She just drives me wild,
so I grabbed her neck--

41:43.250 --> 41:45.669
Gracious me, stop that now!

41:46.962 --> 41:48.172
[Iblis chuckles]

41:48.255 --> 41:49.840
In any case, you mean to say

41:49.924 --> 41:53.636
you came all this way after falling
for each other at first sight?

41:54.220 --> 41:55.054
Falling?

41:56.138 --> 41:57.723
It wasn't a fall. More of a thud. Mmm.

41:58.224 --> 41:59.850
It was totally a thud. Ha.

42:00.643 --> 42:02.019
Still brings tears to my eyes.

42:04.813 --> 42:05.940
Say your four pillars.

42:06.524 --> 42:07.858
"Four pillars"? What's that?

42:07.942 --> 42:11.320
The day you were born.
It's best if you know the time too.

42:13.322 --> 42:17.368
The day I was born, you say?
I was born on a Thursday.

42:18.160 --> 42:20.996
Around 13.8 billion years

42:21.872 --> 42:22.706
BC.

42:22.790 --> 42:24.708
[amusing music playing]

42:27.503 --> 42:30.381
[clicks tongue]
No need to call me "sir" though.

42:34.552 --> 42:36.303
Let me see.

42:36.387 --> 42:39.390
I really should get around
to tending to that field.

42:40.140 --> 42:42.101
[amusing music continues]

42:42.184 --> 42:43.936
[grunting]

42:49.358 --> 42:51.360
[grunting]

42:58.701 --> 43:01.579
Oh Pan-geum might live forever,
but you might not last long.

43:02.454 --> 43:04.290
Here. I brought you a snack.

43:04.873 --> 43:07.084
There's something
I couldn't tell you last time.

43:07.668 --> 43:10.921
My boss asked me
if she and I had also met before.

43:11.005 --> 43:12.965
[panting]

43:15.009 --> 43:16.260
What do you mean by that?

43:17.011 --> 43:19.013
Of course we have. We met just yesterday.

43:19.096 --> 43:22.266
-Not that. I mean, 983 years ago.
-[gasps]

43:23.976 --> 43:25.269
Do you recall that time now?

43:25.352 --> 43:28.355
No. Your master said that he and I
knew each other from the past,

43:28.439 --> 43:30.608
so I wondered if you and I
had also met before.

43:30.691 --> 43:32.234
We did, actually.

43:32.318 --> 43:34.153
But so what if we did?

43:34.653 --> 43:36.447
I want to know what happened.

43:36.530 --> 43:38.782
[enchanting music playing]

43:38.866 --> 43:39.742
Back then…

43:41.744 --> 43:43.078
how did I die?

43:43.162 --> 43:44.038
[sighs]

43:44.955 --> 43:46.373
So she doesn't remember.

43:47.082 --> 43:48.792
She only cares about how she died.

43:49.668 --> 43:51.295
I was locked up because of her.

43:53.005 --> 43:55.633
I spent 983 years thinking only about her.

43:58.052 --> 43:59.928
What were you thinking about?

44:02.014 --> 44:05.768
Whether that lump of clay, near death,
regretted using her wishes on others.

44:06.810 --> 44:10.606
Why am I asking myself that over and over
in this uncomfortable position?

44:10.689 --> 44:12.775
And why do I only have
one piece of furniture?

44:13.275 --> 44:17.154
Hundreds of years passed
as I pondered these three questions.

44:18.030 --> 44:19.031
But the key thing is…

44:19.114 --> 44:22.368
Whatever you say next
better be meaningful.

44:24.495 --> 44:26.246
I still don't know the answers.

44:26.330 --> 44:28.248
Damn it.

44:28.791 --> 44:30.626
Not exactly smart.

44:30.709 --> 44:32.002
Don't you dare tell her

44:32.086 --> 44:34.713
that she made three righteous wishes
before dying, okay?

44:34.797 --> 44:38.801
About her being righteous in every life
after that and… just everything.

44:38.884 --> 44:41.512
Never, okay?
You can't tell the lump of clay.

44:42.012 --> 44:43.514
[Sade] I wouldn't dare tell her.

44:43.597 --> 44:46.225
But do you know
that Master's master is just outside?

44:47.976 --> 44:49.019
[yells]

44:49.728 --> 44:52.481
How much did you hear?

44:53.899 --> 44:55.359
Not exactly observant either.

44:58.028 --> 44:58.862
[Iblis] What the hell?

44:59.446 --> 45:01.031
Why shut the door?

45:02.533 --> 45:06.328
Why are you dressed pretty today?
Hey, Ki Ka-young. Where are you going?

45:06.912 --> 45:08.163
Ki Ka-young!

45:08.247 --> 45:11.166
PSYCHIATRIC CLINIC

45:12.793 --> 45:14.420
Ms. Ki Ka-young, please come in.

45:20.551 --> 45:22.553
[romantic music playing]

45:30.310 --> 45:32.396
[Iblis groans softly, sighs]

45:34.356 --> 45:38.444
Why do I have to carry all this?
I don't feel good. And I'm dizzy.

45:38.527 --> 45:39.778
I'm wearing heels.

45:43.907 --> 45:46.368
I'm going to need
a better reason than that.

45:47.077 --> 45:48.704
[gentle piano music playing]

45:48.787 --> 45:49.997
[Iblis] What are we doing here?

45:50.789 --> 45:54.877
Normal people come to places like this
to eat, take pictures, and such.

46:06.638 --> 46:07.598
Right this way.

46:11.435 --> 46:12.478
[Iblis] Mmm.

46:13.937 --> 46:14.771
Hmm.

46:20.986 --> 46:22.154
Mmm.

46:25.157 --> 46:27.576
[grunts]

46:31.330 --> 46:32.372
Mmm.

46:37.294 --> 46:38.212
Mmm!

46:39.713 --> 46:40.881
Your daily pills.

46:41.465 --> 46:42.925
Do you get them from that place?

46:43.634 --> 46:44.927
Do they make you better?

46:45.010 --> 46:47.638
What do you think?
They're for Grandma's peace of mind.

46:50.140 --> 46:51.141
A few are vitamins.

46:55.103 --> 46:57.814
Why? Were you hoping
the pills would make me better?

46:58.649 --> 47:00.442
Do you always feel like killing me?

47:02.361 --> 47:03.820
Because you're Satan?

47:05.614 --> 47:06.448
[clears throat]

47:07.824 --> 47:08.825
I never said that.

47:10.035 --> 47:10.869
So, what?

47:12.454 --> 47:15.165
You're not normal,
so where do you actually want to go?

47:22.673 --> 47:25.300
[romantic music playing]

47:42.234 --> 47:43.777
Swear you won't push me this time.

47:47.906 --> 47:50.617
[romantic music continues]

48:03.422 --> 48:06.258
You don't think we were caught
on any cameras, do you?

48:07.968 --> 48:08.802
Who knows?

48:14.016 --> 48:15.350
Maybe I will push you.

48:16.977 --> 48:19.896
I don't understand
why you're angry right now.

48:19.980 --> 48:21.523
Right now, you do know.

48:25.861 --> 48:28.572
[Iblis] It's nice that you can
find comfort somewhere.

48:28.655 --> 48:31.199
I guess this is one perk
of owning the lamp.

48:33.243 --> 48:37.122
It's dark up here, so maybe it'd be harder
to see that I'm devoid of emotions.

48:38.624 --> 48:40.292
In that sense, I like you.

48:45.839 --> 48:46.840
Come on,

48:47.758 --> 48:50.177
you can't just drop
something like that on me.

48:55.265 --> 48:56.099
Why exactly

48:57.601 --> 48:58.518
do you like me?

48:59.102 --> 49:00.020
You

49:01.605 --> 49:02.773
are like the cars I fix,

49:02.856 --> 49:06.735
my adjustable wrench, the wheels I roll,
those sorts of things.

49:07.361 --> 49:09.237
I don't need to read your emotions.

49:10.155 --> 49:11.239
You're sturdy.

49:11.865 --> 49:13.116
And sometimes, you shine.

49:13.200 --> 49:14.201
[chuckles]

49:14.284 --> 49:16.328
Of all the things I've owned since birth,

49:16.828 --> 49:20.457
Grandma, Min-ji, the auto shop, my car,

49:21.041 --> 49:22.668
gamja-tang, frogs…

49:23.502 --> 49:25.420
-Frogs?
-The sound of dental scaling…

49:25.504 --> 49:27.839
If I'm this far down the list,
you must not like me.

49:27.923 --> 49:29.675
You haven't even mentioned me yet.

49:31.176 --> 49:32.928
[scoffs] Fine.

49:33.845 --> 49:35.305
I shall try to improve my rank.

49:37.140 --> 49:40.435
Dear Master. Today, I shall gift you
with the greatest darkness.

49:41.019 --> 49:43.855
[distorted chiming]

49:46.316 --> 49:48.819
[echoed thudding]

49:52.447 --> 49:54.658
[wind blowing]

50:09.297 --> 50:11.717
Now we can finally see the stars.
[chuckles]

50:33.613 --> 50:34.489
[gasps]

50:36.950 --> 50:37.993
What?

50:39.119 --> 50:39.953
Do it.

50:42.539 --> 50:43.457
Do what?

50:44.124 --> 50:46.710
When a man says something like
"Let's gaze at the stars,"

50:46.793 --> 50:48.587
then it's 100% the moment to kiss.

50:48.670 --> 50:50.088
It's the moment

50:50.839 --> 50:51.673
for a kiss.

50:55.343 --> 50:56.928
I've always wondered how it feels.

50:57.012 --> 50:58.180
[scoffs]

50:58.263 --> 51:01.850
That's not what this is!
What do you take spirits for? [chuckles]

51:04.394 --> 51:05.437
I won't kiss you.

51:05.520 --> 51:07.230
That's not fair. Why not?

51:07.731 --> 51:09.149
You mentioned the stars!

51:12.778 --> 51:15.447
Fine. Then just stand still.

51:16.198 --> 51:17.282
I'll do it.

51:22.370 --> 51:25.248
-[gulps]
-What's this? Are they usually like this?

51:25.999 --> 51:27.042
No, I--

51:27.125 --> 51:28.877
Don't move. Let me try again.

51:40.430 --> 51:42.349
It still feels exactly the same.

51:45.227 --> 51:46.895
Why do people even like doing this?

51:53.693 --> 51:55.946
[gasps]

51:59.074 --> 51:59.991
Wow.

52:03.161 --> 52:05.205
I really didn't want to do this…

52:09.835 --> 52:10.836
but you're wrong.

52:11.378 --> 52:12.796
It's different when I do it.

52:12.879 --> 52:14.881
[gentle ballad playing]

56:31.137 --> 56:36.142
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi
